=== SECTION 4: CALLBACK CONTRACT ===
function decide(game_state, player_state, history)
    // Returns one Action object per call. Called once per tick per player.
    // game_state: object, player_state: object, history: array of objects

=== SECTION 5: ACTION SPACE ===
5 action types returned as plain objects with a `type` field:
  { type: "Move",   dx: Number, dy: Number, speed: Number }   // speed in [0,1]
  { type: "Pass",   target_pos: [Number, Number], power: Number }
  { type: "Shoot",  angle: Number, power: Number }
  { type: "Tackle", target_player_id: String }
  { type: "Hold" }
Validation rules: non-carrier Pass/Shoot → Hold; out-of-range Tackle → Hold;
speed clamped to [0, 1].

SHOOTING DISCIPLINE (avoid the "dead zone"): if the match log shows your team
took FEW OR ZERO shots despite holding possession and reaching the final third,
your prior strategy has this bug — its pass-first rule releases the ball before
its shoot gate ever fires, so the carrier always passes and never shoots. Fix
it: when the ball carrier is in an attacking position roughly within the top of
the opponent's penalty area (about a fifth of the field from their goal line,
read from field geometry — never hardcoded), reasonably central with a sight of
goal and no defender right on top, SHOOT instead of recycling. Make the shoot
condition OVERLAP the pass-first condition for advanced central carriers — do
not let the shoot gate sit strictly closer to goal. IMPORTANT: change only the
CARRIER's shoot/pass decision; do NOT push extra players up the pitch — that
exposes you to counter-attacks.

OFFSIDE (IFAB Law 11, judged on the x-axis at the moment a team-mate PASSES):
a team-mate is in an offside position if they are strictly inside the
opponents' half AND strictly nearer the opponents' goal line than both the
ball and the second-last opponent (any role — usually GK + last defender).
Level with the second-last opponent = onside. If a player who was in an
offside position when the pass was struck is the FIRST to control that pass,
play stops: free kick to the opposing team at that spot (possession lost).
No offside from goal kicks, throw-ins, or corner kicks.
Tactics: attackers — time runs to stay level with the last defender until
the pass is struck, then sprint. Passers — check the receiver is onside
BEFORE passing forward. Defenders — hold a coordinated high line to trap
goal-hangers.

